<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43254" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sectūra</span></b> , ae, f.
		seco, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a cutting</i> (very rare). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scutum a secturā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 5, § 115</span></i>
			 Müll.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">callaides secturā formantur, alias
					fragiles,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					37, 8, 33, § 111</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A cut</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ut sectura inferior ponatur semper,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					17, 17, 28, § 124</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>The place where any thing is cut</i> or <i>dug</i>, <i>diggings</i>, <i>mines</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aerariae secturaeque,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. G. 3, 21, 3</span></i>
			 (al. structurae).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
